resolved.description:
[s0l0!-header][h1]Arithmetic Operators[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 
The name might be a bit of a giveaway but, [b]Arithmetic operators[/b] pretty much perform arithmetic functions on numbers (both literals and variables). [img id="2745" width="100%"]
Below you can see the [b]addition operator[/b] (+) in action determining the sum of two numbers.[code format="js" codeId="5659"]var x = 10 + 5;
document.write(x);
[/code]
You can add as many numbers or variables together as you want or need to.[code format="js" codeId="5660"]var x = 10;
var y = x + 5 + 22 + 45 + 6548;
document.write(y);
[/code]
[note][b]Heads up![/b]
You can get the result of a string expression using the eval() function, which takes a string expression argument like eval("10 * 20 + 8") and returns the result. If the argument is empty, it returns undefined.[/note]

